  {
    title: "Stage 2: The Claim - Submission and Evaluation",
    category: "claim_process",
    summary: "Submitting the claim and navigating the evaluation process",
    keywords: ["stage", "2", "claim", "submission", "evaluation", "approval"],
    source: "LTC Insurance Portal - Strategy",
    content: `Stage 2 begins when you submit the complete claims packet to the insurance company. This is the formal evaluation phase.

Key tasks in Stage 2:
1. **Complete claim packet** - Fill out all required forms accurately and completely
2. **Attach all documents** - Submit ALL documentation in ONE packet (never in pieces)
3. **Include policy number** - Ensure policy number appears on every page of submitted documents
4. **Prepare for assessment** - Be ready for the third-party RN evaluation
5. **Understand review period** - The insurance company typically has 30 days to review and make a decision

The 30-day review period:
- Insurance company reviews all submitted documentation
- Third-party RN conducts in-person assessment
- Case manager evaluates medical necessity
- Insurance company makes approval or denial decision
- You are notified of decision in writing

Important guidelines:
- Submit ALL documents together in one packet
- Never submit documents in pieces or over time
- Ensure consistency between all submitted documents
- Policy number must appear on every page
- Keep copies of everything you submit
- Track submission date and follow up if no response within 30 days

If approved: You move to Stage 3
If denied: You have the right to appeal (though appeal success rates are low)

Duration: 30 days for initial decision, plus time for any appeals.`,
